## Conversation
User asked to enable "claude fable" (claude-fable-5, served via GitHub
Copilot) as the default in the litellm config. After the first delivery
they hit a 400 "Invalid model name passed in model=claude-fable-5" from
Claude Code, which turned into a debugging session. Finally they asked
to commit using the conventional-commits skill.

## Actions
- Added claude-fable-5 to configs/litellm/config.yaml model_list as
  github_copilot/claude-fable-5, copying the other Copilot Claude
  entries (drop thinking, *copilot_headers alias)
- Switched DEFAULT_LITELLM_MODEL in local-bin/litellm-proxy.sh from
  claude-opus-4-8 to claude-fable-5; updated README.md to match
- shellfmt.sh passed; validated YAML anchor expansion with yq
- Ran litellm-proxy.sh restart (container was up 6 days on stale
  config), then verified: models lists claude-fable-5, and a
  /v1/messages test request returned "ok"

## Errors & Mistakes
- First delivery only edited files and did not restart the proxy, which
  caused the user-visible 400 error
- docker volume ls --format '{{.CreatedAt}}' is not supported on this
  docker; use docker volume inspect instead
- python3 here has no yaml module; use yq for YAML checks

## Dead Ends
- Suspected prisma migrations wiped DB-stored models during the image
  update; disproved — all migrations were additive and _prisma_migrations
  shows the DB continuous since 2026-08-18

## Hints for Future Agents
- LiteLLM reads the bind-mounted config.yaml only at startup; any config
  change needs litellm-proxy.sh restart to take effect
- restart also applies pending pinned image digest updates (renovate)
- Volumes: DB is litellm_litellm-db-data (compose project prefix),
  Copilot OAuth is external litellm-copilot-data and survives restarts
- A post-commit hook autopushes master and rebases on rejection, so the
  commit SHA can change immediately (365cdc5 -> 162d46b here); attach
  notes to the final SHA

## Codebase Discoveries
- wandb/deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro was listed by the old container but
  exists nowhere durable: never in config.yaml git history and every DB
  model table (LiteLLM_ProxyModelTable, LiteLLM_ModelTable,
  LiteLLM_Config) is empty. It was in-memory only and is gone after the
  restart
- Bug: get_litellm_salt_key() in litellm-proxy.sh is defined but never
  called; run_compose starts LiteLLM with a blank LITELLM_SALT_KEY
  (LiteLLM then falls back to the master key for encrypting DB
  credentials). Possibly why the UI-added model never persisted
- LITELLM_MODEL env var overrides the default without a code change

